---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const designAreas = [
  {
    title: "1. State of formation",
    description:
      "We determine which U.S. state is most suitable for forming your LLC based on your business activity, location, customers, costs, and obligations.",
  },
  {
    title: "2. Tax treatment",
    description:
      "We analyze how your LLC should be taxed and which tax classification may be best suited to your structure and business model.",
  },
  {
    title: "3. Management structure",
    description:
      "We determine whether your LLC should operate under a Member-Managed or Manager-Managed model, depending on who will manage and represent the company.",
  },
  {
    title: "4. Accounting method",
    description:
      "We review whether your records should be maintained on a Cash Basis or Accrual Basis, according to the characteristics of your operations.",
  },
  {
    title: "5. Level of confidentiality",
    description:
      "We evaluate the level of privacy your structure may offer and what owner or manager information could be disclosed depending on the state and applicable obligations.",
  },
  {
    title: "6. Business activity code",
    description:
      "We identify the code that best represents your business activity so it can be used correctly in the corresponding registrations and forms.",
  },
];

const meetingTopics = [
  "Business activity",
  "Owners’ place of residence",
  "Countries from which the company will operate",
  "Type of customers",
  "Estimated revenue",
  "Payment methods",
  "Banking operations",
  "Members and managers",
  "Business outlook",
];

const recommendations = [
  "State of formation",
  "Tax treatment",
  "Management structure",
  "Accounting method",
  "Level of confidentiality",
  "Business activity code",
];
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main
    class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 text-slate-700 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 dark:text-slate-200"
  >
    <header class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
      <p
        class="text-secundario mb-3 text-sm font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase"
      >
        Strategic planning
      </p>
      <h1
        class="text-primario-black text-3xl font-bold sm:text-5xl dark:text-white"
      >
        LLC Planning and Design
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8">
        Design first. Form later. Define how your LLC will operate before
        starting the formation process.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="design-areas">
      <h2
        id="design-areas"
        class="text-primario-black text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl dark:text-white"
      >
        Six decisions we analyze with you
      </h2>
      <div class="mt-7 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          designAreas.map((area) => (
            <article class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-6 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900">
              <h3 class="text-primario-black text-lg font-semibold dark:text-white">
                {area.title}
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-3 leading-7">{area.description}</p>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="bg-primario-black mt-14 rounded-3xl p-7 text-white sm:p-10"
      aria-labelledby="design-first"
    >
      <h2 id="design-first" class="text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl">
        Do not form first and resolve questions later
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-200">
        Our approach starts with a simple idea: <strong class="text-white"
          >first we design the structure, and then we form it.</strong
        >
      </p>
      <p class="mt-7">During a virtual meeting, we analyze factors such as:</p>
      <ul class="mt-5 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          meetingTopics.map((topic) => (
            <li class="rounded-xl border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-3">
              {topic}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-7 leading-7 text-slate-200">
        With this information, we can explain and advise you on how an LLC would
        work specifically for your situation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="deliverables">
      <h2
        id="deliverables"
        class="text-primario-black text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl dark:text-white"
      >
        What do you receive?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        At the end of the service, you will receive an <strong
          >LLC Planning and Design Report</strong
        >, which includes:
      </p>
      <div class="mt-7 space-y-5">
        <article class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <h3 class="text-primario-black text-xl font-semibold dark:text-white">
            1. Summary of your situation
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
            We compile the main elements analyzed during the consultation so you
            have a clear view of your structure and operating model.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <h3 class="text-primario-black text-xl font-semibold dark:text-white">
            2. Recommended design for your LLC
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
            We present our recommendations regarding:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">
            {
              recommendations.map((recommendation) => (
                <li class="flex gap-2">
                  <>
                    <span class="text-secundario" aria-hidden="true">
                      ✓
                    </span>
                    <span>{recommendation}</span>
                  </>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">
            Everything is tailored to your business activity and particular
            circumstances.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="rounded-2xl bg-slate-50 p-6 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <h3 class="text-primario-black text-xl font-semibold dark:text-white">
            3. Your main tax obligations
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
            We include an explanation of the main forms and obligations that may
            apply to your LLC before the IRS.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
            Not all LLCs file the same forms or have the same obligations. These
            may vary depending on who the owners are, where they reside, how the
            company is taxed, and what type of operations it conducts.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
            Our goal is for you to understand these obligations before you begin
            operating.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="mt-14 border-y border-slate-200 py-10 dark:border-slate-700"
      aria-labelledby="informed-decision"
    >
      <h2
        id="informed-decision"
        class="text-primario-black text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl dark:text-white"
      >
        Make your decision with clarity
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        Once you receive your report, you will have a much more complete
        understanding of how your LLC would operate from the following
        perspectives:
      </p>
      <p
        class="text-primario-black mt-5 text-center text-lg font-semibold tracking-wide dark:text-white"
      >
        Legal · Tax · Corporate · Accounting · Banking · Operational
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 leading-7">
        This will help you decide with greater confidence whether an LLC is
        appropriate for your business and how it should be formed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="border-secundario/30 bg-secundario/10 mt-14 rounded-3xl border p-7 sm:p-10"
      aria-labelledby="continue-formation"
    >
      <h2
        id="continue-formation"
        class="text-primario-black text-2xl font-bold sm:text-3xl dark:text-white"
      >
        Would you like to continue with the formation?
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 leading-7">
        If you decide to move forward with us after the planning stage, you can
        upgrade to any of our formation plans.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        The amount paid for Planning and Design is credited toward the process,
        so you will only need to pay the difference for the plan you select.
      </p>
      <h3 class="text-primario-black mt-8 text-xl font-bold dark:text-white">
        Design first. Form later.
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-7">
        Avoid creating an LLC without first understanding how it will be taxed,
        what obligations it will have, or whether the selected structure truly
        fits your business.
      </p>
      <p class="text-primario-black mt-5 text-lg font-semibold dark:text-white">
        Schedule your LLC Planning and Design consultation and build your
        structure with greater clarity from the start.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
